      "sourceCount": 1,
      "datePrecision": "day",
      "dateRaw": "2025-11-05",
      "summary": "**First malware families observed calling an LLM at runtime**. **PROMPTSTEAL** was used by Russia's **APT28 (FROZENLAKE)** **in live operations against Ukraine**, calling **Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct** through the Hugging Face API to generate commands dynamically; **PROMPTFLUX** (first seen 2025-06) is a VBScript dropper that calls the Gemini API for obfuscation and evasion techniques, and **is still in development/testing, without real compromise capability**. Attackers were also found using pretexts such as \"CTF student\" and \"security researcher\" to bypass Gemini guardrails",
